**Read:** [Oxygen Pipeline and Piping Systems — EIGA Doc 13/20](../sources/Oxygen-Pipeline-and-Piping-Systems-EIGA.lingua#r_7BBE969N5JQJES1KG9AKNBEZBV), the entire Doc 13/20 and actual referenced methods used; [Good practices guide for loading and unloading of cryogenic liquid tankers — AIGA](../sources/Cryogenic-Liquid-Tanker-Transfers-AIGA.lingua#r_52MNR8Y6S0N1MXDSX8F3XF424C), the complete tanker-transfer guide; [Inorganic Chemical Technology — Nanda Kishore, NPTEL](../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/sources/Inorganic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_77Z8T5RFYFNNXZ7XKZFKPRKDKR), the complete relevant manufacturing progression; [Graduate Logistics Systems — MIT ESD.260J](../sources/Graduate-Logistics-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_4NMCCS7JPNK6CD9V9Z4XTQPKR8), the full applicable inventory/transport/network methods.

Choose oxygen, nitrogen or another documented gas and specify composition/contaminants, state, flow/pressure, variability, continuity and the user's actual operation. Read the complete manufacturing/separation material and whole applicable gas-industry technical guides. For oxygen, derive the complete material/cleanliness and operating argument from the actual EIGA publication rather than applying a generic piping rule.

Compare pipeline, bulk liquid with local vaporisation, packaged supply and on-site generation where technically relevant. Develop a complete source-to-use boundary including conditioning, analysis, reserve, utilities, delivery access, maintenance and trained responsibility. Model usable quantities with explicit pressure/temperature/compressibility or phase/property methods appropriate to the case.

Investigate a missed delivery, failure of a shared service, contaminated supply and return from maintenance. Distinguish theoretical reserve contents from deliverable accepted reserve at the needed rate. Compare quantity/service/cost and resource consequences with uncertainty, and test the smallest models independently. Read full primary methods for every physical property, qualification or design claim.

Produce a substantial engineering/research account and have the case challenged on its weakest interface. Revise the proposal and state exactly what public-case reconstruction, supplied-data calculation or actual supervised work establishes. The intended achievement is a defended understanding of a qualified gas service and its alternatives; it does not conflate documentary study with commissioning or operating an installation.

